{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.LadderPhaseMirrorCovariance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderPhaseMirrorCovariance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ZBarParity","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.CrossingWeightAffine"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.phaseTwice_eq_counit_sub_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.phaseTwice_eq_counit_sub_trace","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseMirrorCovariance.lean#L269-L288","doc":"**The ladder's doubled phase IS the counit-minus-trace gap.** With the Q_β\nevaluation map `E(w) = h²/2 − h·w` of `CrossingWeightAffine` (`w = 1` the\nFrobenius counit `ε`, `w = z` the Markov trace `tr_M`):\n\n  `2·α = phaseTwice z h = E(1) − E(z) = ε(Δ) − tr_M(Δ)`.\n\nSo the ladder eigenphase `α = (z−1)h/2` is not an arbitrary\nparameterisation: it is exactly **half the counit-minus-trace gap**, i.e. the\ninfinitesimal generator of the counit→trace transport. This *locates* the one\nunjustified step of the Q_β ladder — the exponentiation of this gap into\n`cos(α − u/2)`, axiomatised as `QOU.Interactions.QBetaCosResummation` — as\nthe target a convention-D re-derivation must actually supply (the transport),\nrather than a new phase *formula*. The identity holds for **any** `z`, so it\nis convention-blind; it *locates*, it closes nothing numerical — the c_k rung\nvalues remain anti-fit-fenced (bean `qou-cds1`). One `ring` line over\n`CrossingWeightAffine.evalMap_affine`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zD_bar_mean_eq_loop_mean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zD_bar_mean_eq_loop_mean","kind":"theorem","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseMirrorCovariance.lean#L260-L267","doc":"**Under D the bar-mean and the loop-mean coincide**:\n`z_D + bar(z_D) = 2 z_D - h = loopMeanTwice z_D h`. Symmetrising over the\nmirror and symmetrising over the crossing sign are the same operation in\nthis frame — which is why the §3 projection has no residual freedom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zD_bar_eq_negative_loop","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zD_bar_eq_negative_loop","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseMirrorCovariance.lean#L251-L258","doc":"**Under convention D, bar sends `z` to the negative-stabilisation loop\nvalue.** `bar(z_D) = z_D - h`. Mirroring a link exchanges positive and\nnegative crossings, hence exchanges the two stabilisation moves, and D's\nMarkov parameter tracks that exchange exactly. (Convention C's does not:\n`z_C` is bar-fixed, so `bar(z_C) - (z_C - h) = h ≠ 0`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.phaseTwice_projected_eq_loopMean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.phaseTwice_projected_eq_loopMean","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseMirrorCovariance.lean#L242-L249","doc":"**The §3 projection is the phase at the mean loop value, not a shift.**\n`2·(2 alpha) - h² = (loopMeanTwice z h - 2)·h`, i.e. removing the bar\nanomaly from `alpha = (z-1)h/2` gives exactly `((z + (z-h))/2 - 1)·h/2` —\nthe same formula with the positive-stabilisation loop value `z` replaced by\nthe mean of the two. Pure `ring`, true in any `CommRing` and for any `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.loopMeanTwice","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.loopMeanTwice","kind":"def","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseMirrorCovariance.lean#L238-L240","doc":"Twice the mean of the two Markov stabilisation loop values `z` and `z - h`:\n`loopMeanTwice z h = 2z - h`. Kept doubled so §4 stays division-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.phaseTwiceD_sub_hsq_bar_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.phaseTwiceD_sub_hsq_bar_odd","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseMirrorCovariance.lean#L192-L204","doc":"**The bar-odd part of the D-frame phase is `2 alpha_D - h²/2`**, i.e.\n`alpha_D - h²/4`.\n\nSubtracting half the anomaly is the unique shift that makes the phase\nmirror-covariant, so this projection is *forced* by §1 + `zD_sub_bar_eq_h`\nrather than chosen. Note `bar(h²) = h²` (`h` bar-odd ⇒ `h²` bar-even), so\nthe same constant is subtracted on both sides — that is what makes the\nshift consistent, and it is why no freedom remains. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.phaseTwiceD_bar_anomaly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.phaseTwiceD_bar_anomaly","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseMirrorCovariance.lean#L182-L190","doc":"**The D-frame phase bar-anomaly is exactly `h²`** (for the doubled phase;\nequivalently `bar(alpha_D) + alpha_D = h²/2`). Immediate from §1 and\n`zD_sub_bar_eq_h`, with `h = q - q⁻¹`. The numerical value measured in\n`qbeta-eigenphase-branch-and-barodd-projection.witness.json` is this\nclosed form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zD_sub_bar_eq_h","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zD_sub_bar_eq_h","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseMirrorCovariance.lean#L163-L180","doc":"**`z_D` is not bar-fixed, and its anomaly is exactly `h = q - q⁻¹`.**\n\n`z_D(q) - z_D(q⁻¹) = q - q⁻¹`, an exact identity, not an approximation:\n`q³/(q²+1) - q⁻¹/(1+q²)·... = (q⁴-1)/(q(1+q²)) = (q²-1)/q = q - q⁻¹`.\n\nThis is the single fact that makes the whole D-frame phase story\ndeterministic — combined with §1 it fixes the anomaly with no freedom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zD","kind":"def","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseMirrorCovariance.lean#L159-L161","doc":"The convention-D Markov parameter: `z_D = q³/(q² + 1)` (owner ruling\n2026-08-15, canonical). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.phaseTwiceC_bar_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.phaseTwiceC_bar_odd","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseMirrorCovariance.lean#L147-L155","doc":"**The convention-C ladder phase is bar-ODD** — and by structure, not by\ncoincidence: it is `phaseTwice_bar_odd_iff_z_bar_fixed` fed with\n`zC_bar_fixed`. A framing phase must be bar-odd (writhe is mirror-odd,\n`WritheMarkovInvariance.writhe_inv`), so convention C passes that test. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zC_bar_fixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zC_bar_fixed","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseMirrorCovariance.lean#L140-L145","doc":"**`z_C` is exactly bar-fixed**: `z_C(s⁻¹) = z_C(s)`. This is\n`QOU.QBeta.z_bar_invariant_field` (PR #3449) restated on `zC`; only\n`s ≠ 0` is needed, since when `1 + s² = 0` both sides are `0` under\nMathlib's division convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zC","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseMirrorCovariance.lean#L136-L138","doc":"The convention-C Markov parameter in the half-power coordinate `s`\n(`s² = q`): `z_C = s/(1 + s²) = √q/(1+q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.phaseTwice_bar_odd_iff_z_bar_fixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.phaseTwice_bar_odd_iff_z_bar_fixed","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseMirrorCovariance.lean#L114-L130","doc":"**Mirror-covariance of the phase characterises bar-invariance of `z`.**\nOver a domain with `h ≠ 0`, the doubled phase is bar-ODD (its bar image is\nits negative) **iff** `z` is exactly bar-fixed. The forward direction is\nthe structural exclusion this file exists to state: a convention whose\nMarkov parameter moves under bar cannot carry a mirror-covariant framing\nphase, whatever the size of the movement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.phaseTwice_bar_anomaly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.phaseTwice_bar_anomaly","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseMirrorCovariance.lean#L99-L112","doc":"**The bar-anomaly of the phase is `h` times the bar-anomaly of `z`.**\n\n`h` is bar-ODD (`bar h = -h`, immediate for `h = q - q⁻¹`), so applying bar\nto `2 alpha = (z - 1) h` sends `z ↦ zb` and `h ↦ -h`. The sum with the\nunbarred phase is then\n\n  `phaseTwice zb (-h) + phaseTwice z h = h * (z - zb)`.\n\nEverything downstream in this file is a specialisation of this one `ring`\nidentity: the phase's failure to be mirror-covariant is *exactly* the\nMarkov parameter's failure to be bar-invariant, amplified by `h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.phaseTwice","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.phaseTwice","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseMirrorCovariance.lean#L94-L97","doc":"The doubled ladder phase `2·alpha = (z - 1)·h`, carrying no division so\nthe parity bookkeeping is available in any `CommRing` (including\ncharacteristic 2, where `alpha` itself would not be defined). ","signatureChunk":0}]}